                <invention-title lang="de">BI-VORHERSAGE FÜR DIE VIDEOCODIERUNG</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">BI-PRÉDICTION POUR CODAGE VIDÉO</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">BI-PREDICTION FOR VIDEO CODING</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Systems, methods, and instrumentalities may be provided for determining whether to bypass bidirectional optical flow (BDOF) if BDOF is used in combination with bi-prediction with coding unit (CU) weights (e.g., generalized bi-prediction (GBi)). A coding system may combine coding modes, coding techniques, and/or coding tools. The coding system may include a wireless transmit/receive unit (WTRU). For example, the coding system may combine BDOF and bi-prediction with CU weights (BCW). BDOF may include refining a motion vector associated with a current CU based at least in part on gradients associated with a location in the current CU. The coding system may determine that BDOF is enabled, and/or that bi-prediction with CU weights is enabled for the current CU. The coding system's determination that bi-prediction with CU weights is enabled and/or that BDOF is enabled may be based on one or more indications.</p>
            </abstract>
